[{"id":"VRCE-1-48-1","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":1,"english":"And having been deprived of his scrotum, Śakra with eyes tremulous with fear, addressed the celestials with Agni at their head, as well as he Siddhas and the Gandharvas and the Cāraņas, saying,","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.635,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048001","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9b7d5de2b068063912971509b167d44e5e151be060c26b115954237e309a9b17","compact":"d2ddb5b38d696775a81d0cf699b30392019b10a7d9008e97a2f58ff500e17e14","nasal":"d2ddb5b38d696775a81d0cf699b30392019b10a7d9008e97a2f58ff500e17e14"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-2","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":2,"english":"I have accomplished the work of the celestials by stirring the ire of the high-souled Gautama, and thereby disturbing his austerities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048002","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"59dc1705dbbd342262320d82133dfe704cf72f7bb8c94adb6450a980150a98dc","compact":"9db3ab4d8b7a4f3864199b53b8ef5bcee35a539a5405728323a6d37511ff5291","nasal":"9db3ab4d8b7a4f3864199b53b8ef5bcee35a539a5405728323a6d37511ff5291"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-3","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":3,"english":"And in doing so, I have been deprived of my scrotum; and Ahalyā also has been put down. And I have deprived him of his ascetic energy by causing him to utter a mighty curse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048003","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9f1c9e680ec093c9bc52526fc5c3741c6a518ec823f850082b55589b62d09fb5","compact":"f2df122a3d10964e3c6b7d4553c2c2feb0f77394317b45511a27a71af1259c39","nasal":"f2df122a3d10964e3c6b7d4553c2c2feb0f77394317b45511a27a71af1259c39"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-4","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":4,"english":"And, therefore, you celestials, and saints, and Cāraņas, you should restore my scrotum to me who have served the gods.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.517,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048004","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"dcd344a16913cadfe62e216ef058eb42fa0b334d8f1596614f3fc41cba67ea9f","compact":"b9c8ae9b4c3e47bc4beca03584f09527b36a33a6420406bdf399af124359e198","nasal":"b9c8ae9b4c3e47bc4beca03584f09527b36a33a6420406bdf399af124359e198"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-5","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":5,"english":"Hearing Satakratu's (performer of an hundred sacrifices, one of the appellations of Indra). The manes of ancestors. words, the deities along with the Maruts led by Agni, presented themselves before the divine Pitrs. And then Agni addressed the latter, saying.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.783,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048005","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3a031753f1eb9ace3256d03dbcceb5dcf2ae8350012537cf3a123b8566c3b08d","compact":"f8444db3634a48d35ec3ba2295de618657c9860f9ec9b1d35c6d1dbadcc48b0e","nasal":"f8444db3634a48d35ec3ba2295de618657c9860f9ec9b1d35c6d1dbadcc48b0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-6","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":6,"english":"This ram is possessed of a scrotum; while Śakra has been deprived of his. Do you taking the scrotum of the ram furnish Sakra with it.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048006","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7010e1c917415d4fd2cfbce4ef6272616e946afd683c995f1c1be635bf163d20","compact":"87f0fe582f3161d687bab70a4f991ff2b18973fcb16d25215486081798cfcd8f","nasal":"87f0fe582f3161d687bab70a4f991ff2b18973fcb16d25215486081798cfcd8f"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-7","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":7,"english":"And although deprived of the scrotum, the will be able to grant consummate satisfaction to you. And on those that will offer such a ram for your entertainment, you will bestow undying and profuse merit.'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048007","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7454f50a395776af0e756791c37a609f79749029b68fb6d55d84e3e166b6575a","compact":"30ea0d54df3cc14f20623a5b9b19380ba0eceb5f16108486669796f0405168fd","nasal":"f061b7f9213ff763b811d31b033d87276a6af7677172b045892482fa71ffc742"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-8","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":8,"english":"ram Hearing Agni's speech, the assembled Pitrs, rooting up the scrotum of the ram, joined it to the person of the thousand-eyed deity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.908,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048008","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8cb253e7166db8ffbb95d95c81468bc00e86b91ce21c1fcd081ce4f5f4dff232","compact":"5c2be94ebf6ca2d433c81ed70f735e2c8118793364d8dc8eba5a33ced0689771","nasal":"5c2be94ebf6ca2d433c81ed70f735e2c8118793364d8dc8eba5a33ced0689771"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-9","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":9,"english":"Thence forth, O Kākutstha, the divine Pitrs together feast upon scrotumless rams, for their scrotum had been joined to the person of Indra.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048009","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d8f3be72b9db13db81d42be59be13f88a71dafdd7e9222b866a45fec0a1f2b97","compact":"506536641ba9ed8cf25766d31f4669b275c298875bb03433d56bef4cc5ffbbab","nasal":"a9b9708b85aa8a2a2311a44287e85d2fa11bf3c6e7fbf5a78f83ab0139854979"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-10","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":10,"english":"Thenceforth, O Rāghava, Indra also through the high-souled Gautama's ascetic energy, has been bearing the scrotum of a ram.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.764,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048010","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"505d3252c5b24eed59ec82c4a4afb82edea8c261e8298995eea22debb00a4eb0","compact":"49bf15e8942a91e8aa86c75314728ddb3724904baad489ea1fffc2d7bdb31d69","nasal":"be778ecbeb0fca0d6660f817cc31535c19bf1e152e36079027ed8594d3926b14"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-11","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":11,"english":"Therefore, O highly powerful one, do you enter into the hermitage of that pious one, and deliver the dignified and divinely fair Ahalyā.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048011","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1608f7fbb049643733ce1422f9d3a9d9ae698e8c27097d705fdf34373fefa563","compact":"09bb6b74a06aca90eb1e2806d094482f3365637f4b41d138b025fa428a0482b4","nasal":"09bb6b74a06aca90eb1e2806d094482f3365637f4b41d138b025fa428a0482b4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-12","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":12,"english":"On hearing Viśvāmitra's words, Rāghava in company with Lakşmaņa, placing Viśvāmitra in their front, entered the asylum.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048012","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e2f4795d2da36926cbd38034c7a9dc50d7e97f524d850772c8ace785f2c08295","compact":"72a4584faeeda03fcb0f75fd93aec800229b1833461e3a0693a55e3b06b27d16","nasal":"72a4584faeeda03fcb0f75fd93aec800229b1833461e3a0693a55e3b06b27d16"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-13","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":13,"english":"They beheld that magnificent dame flaming in ascetic energy; and incapable of being gazed at too near even by the celestials and the Asuras; as if created by the Deity to be the divinely charming Woman; like a flame hid in smoke; or the brightness of the full moon clouded and dimmed in mist; or the solar splendour incapable of being beheld of account of clouds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048013","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"92ccc54b45d49d22028430b2470832c4f2eed82a195ee8007cdbdf4a32821462","compact":"9cd9a38a370dc532092ee3d25d439a16f5f04877ff570f11c63d14337df8c9bc","nasal":"9cd9a38a370dc532092ee3d25d439a16f5f04877ff570f11c63d14337df8c9bc"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-14","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":14,"english":"They beheld that magnificent dame flaming in ascetic energy; and incapable of being gazed at too near even by the celestials and the Asuras; as if created by the Deity to be the divinely charming Woman; like a flame hid in smoke; or the brightness of the full moon clouded and dimmed in mist; or the solar splendour incapable of being beheld of account of clouds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048014","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"2e5127f5cd7b8f3a0480ff65f84039163b3070871ac30ca7bdc575887232b3e3","compact":"7782d1e78420f7300c077e7c3d1669037aa89e263bef31fb79bf35ff79b554ec","nasal":"1ea68facaabf2eec93bebff158929abc5c85edf1a36259bdfe9c8a26c324645a"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-15","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":15,"english":"They beheld that magnificent dame flaming in ascetic energy; and incapable of being gazed at too near even by the celestials and the Asuras; as if created by the Deity to be the divinely charming Woman; like a flame hid in smoke; or the brightness of the full moon clouded and dimmed in mist; or the solar splendour incapable of being beheld of account of clouds.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048015","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c28a2e473ebfe047fc9e6b2374dd601b2bd13e0d8690118f80cc6c5714b37e30","compact":"89ca540508bce68e22254e755ad563601c33e7d43f25f72b2735a9108f78bec0","nasal":"766267ae1bd79f91e5fdd81a1d30ab865f95f7043d9714cc7ceec5322eb3be03"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-16","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":16,"english":"And by virtue of Gautama's word, she had been incapable of being seen by any in the three worlds, till the sight of Rāma. And now the curse having come to an end, she could be perceived by them.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.984,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048016","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"bf9624bc03d5173ea3dc39e0aea2e7766e31260c7b3dbf6da0681dab38ed4bdf","compact":"ccdc43d0eeeeaa7cdd1e26f2d81e55c00393ebecc73c18fbf608b1d2556a0ec7","nasal":"ccdc43d0eeeeaa7cdd1e26f2d81e55c00393ebecc73c18fbf608b1d2556a0ec7"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-17","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":17,"english":"The two descendants of Raghu then took hold of her feet; but remembering Gautama's words, she on her part took hold of theirs. And with a collected mind she gave them water for their feet as well as Arghya, and extended to them the rites of hospitality.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.661,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048017","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"32a4882339ed411906f2f846ab370309e38943199d84630e428c2a5a30d6866c","compact":"f9a843b9b8191865d5937e5ee0b099c20e88d004335445f2dea35df7499710d2","nasal":"937136c5c49035d650319bae3e9067ce24a6ac2c8628bb9e29085efd892aabf4"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-18","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":18,"english":"The two descendants of Raghu then took hold of her feet; but remembering Gautama's words, she on her part took hold of theirs. And with a collected mind she gave them water for their feet as well as Arghya, and extended to them the rites of hospitality.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.892,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048018","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f99ab0f650fa24f0e901298e40025312d9ddbeaaefd7714bfbe10cc6e826822","compact":"6e07c6fd54acefdaac5be75fc17c7211354496073c7c3d9bf9ffa5a640e09e95","nasal":"6e07c6fd54acefdaac5be75fc17c7211354496073c7c3d9bf9ffa5a640e09e95"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-19","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":19,"english":"And the Kākutstha accepted the homage thus rendered according to the ordinance. And blossoms began to shower copiously to the sounds of kettledrums; and the Gandharvas and the Apsaras began to rejoice greatly.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.696,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048019","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6c63590555122525ee80379e59ee7072e730aa6bf444cd6367b13eda2c2fb5ca","compact":"2065bb4757f0760493ce2647ff49cf0fdf506e30a92ebb30fd86ac5fa9fd3bd6","nasal":"a62ed45025ebaee9caa46cfce41b5f0818e7b8caa54369abe7c65364bdc2f231"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-20","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":20,"english":"And exclaiming, 'Excellent, excellent,' the celestials honoured Ahalyā, as with as person purified by penance, she again come under Gautama's governance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048020","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5168747df6c33d2cce4361e71b9d666b40272176281ea4a41e3e3d91b49d6d8e","compact":"5b101c83148f1e321c0030d9a9d7f5ebf095d4788429a86e858b63f81b60399e","nasal":"5240f564a499c98898044d213218352f70cbc2875608115e5775e025ed6b4206"}},{"id":"VRCE-1-48-21","kanda":1,"kandaId":"bala","sarga":48,"verse":21,"english":"And the highly energetic Gautama also happy on his union with Ahalyā, honoured Rāma highly, and that one of mighty mortifications then became engaged in austerities.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.855,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-1-49-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"1048021","sanskritFile":"Ram01.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7cf4dd896b98defe3bbd48a52e78f01f453c4028313db39d2d849762db9da406","compact":"d112df2bf882